    "oracle": {
      "description_paragraphs": [
        "At round $t$, choose an arm $X_t$ using the past and an independent random seed; then observe both coordinates $(Y_t^1,Y_t^2)$. Each coordinate is conditionally 1-sub-Gaussian around its fixed mean: $\\mathbb E[\\exp(\\theta(Y_t^i-\\mu^i(X_t)))\\mid\\mathcal H_{t-1},X_t]\\le\\exp(\\theta^2/2)$. Independence between coordinates is not required. There is no feedback for unselected arms and no sample reuse interface.",
        "The public inputs are $K,T$ and, for a probability guarantee, $\\delta$. The means and primary-optimal set are hidden."
      ],
      "operation": "At round $t$, choose an arm $X_t$ using the past and an independent random seed; then observe both coordinates $(Y_t^1,Y_t^2)$. Each coordinate is conditionally 1-sub-Gaussian around its fixed mean: $\\mathbb E[\\exp(\\theta(Y_t^i-\\mu^i(X_t)))\\mid\\mathcal H_{t-1},X_t]\\le\\exp(\\theta^2/2)$. Independence between coordinates is not required. There is no feedback for unselected arms and no sample reuse interface. The public inputs are $K,T$ and, for a probability guarantee, $\\delta$. The means and primary-optimal set are hidden.",
